menu "tinywarden"

choice TW_LED_KIND
    prompt "LED on GPIO48"
    default TW_LED_PLAIN
    help
        What the board has on GPIO48. The ESP32-S3 SuperMini used for development has a plain LED
        there (it shows red). Some other boards have a WS2812 RGB LED. Driving a plain LED with WS2812
        data only makes it glow faintly without blinking.

config TW_LED_PLAIN
    bool "Plain LED, on when the pin is high"

config TW_LED_WS2812
    bool "WS2812 RGB LED"
endchoice

config TW_DEV_DOWNLOAD_ENDPOINT
    bool "Development: allow rebooting into download mode over the network"
    default n
    help
        Adds POST /tw/dev/download-mode, which reboots the chip into the ROM download mode so it can be
        flashed without pressing BOOT+RST. Anything on the Mac can call it, and download mode lets the
        flash be read, so never enable this on a device that holds a real vault.

config TW_DEV_SKIP_BUTTON
    bool "Development: do not wait for the BOOT button (auto-approve)"
    default n
    help
        Registration, login and wipe are approved without the button, so tests can run unattended.
        Never enable this on a device that holds a real vault.

endmenu
